            <ArticleTitle>Recognition and treatment of right ventricular myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>69-73, 100</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thirty to 50% of patients experiencing an inferior wall infarct may also have involvement of the right ventricle. Right ventricular infarctions seldom exist alone they are almost always seen with an inferior infarct. The coronary artery involved is usually an occluded right coronary artery (RCA).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
